lines += ['','## Changes applied and unchanged controls','','- Reuse the exact tested `edges.mjs` extractor from the angular-example-app analysis: relative ESM imports/re-exports and aliases; scope-aware function bindings; constructor/this/super and inheritance relations; syntactic immediate-function class aliases; statically known object fields; function-value and callback-use relations. The relation extractor receives code, import paths and inventory IDs/spans; ground-truth labels and seeds are loaded only after extraction.','- Add extracted relations to the original local-call/function-argument/containment/sibling graphs. Keep radius one, sibling window two, synchronous oracle promotion, the 18,000-character expansion bound, and the source identity policy. No module-initialization matching or module-membership expansion is added.','- Run a minimal source-relative-ESM ablation, the full improved per-chunk graph, and a separate full cross-chunk graph. A per-chunk baseline control and a cross-chunk-disabled control reproduce the frozen recovered pair sets exactly in every repository.','- Retain ngx-charts\' ten non-one-to-one supported cases in denominators and leave them unrecovered in every variant; do not choose arbitrary identities or remove hard cases. No changes to source parsing, target selection, labels or seed thresholds.','- Bare-package entry resolution is still not implemented. The source-relative-ESM probe handles available relative re-export chains, but imports such as rxjs package subpaths, tslib, lit and other package entries can remain unresolved. See coverage.json. Dynamic properties, general function return/argument flow and complex CommonJS/factory behavior remain bounded-analysis gaps.','- Cross-chunk analysis uses only the frozen prepared target-containing chunks: RealWorld 3, angular-example-app 11, ngx-charts 2. Other emitted chunks are not loaded as analysis units. Identical saved chunk bytes are recognized through artifact-hash aliases. This is not a complete runtime-loaded project graph.','- No ranking, validation, embeddings, model cache, or model endpoint is used. Oracle-promoted correct pairs can still benefit from approximate or extraneous graph edges; zero recovered-pair regressions do not establish static-edge precision or future model-assisted precision.','','## Main observations','','- RxJS is the largest beneficiary in all three repositories: RealWorld 30/346 → 334/346; angular-example-app 26/291 → 281/291; ngx-charts 32/346 → 331/346.','- Gains are not universal: RealWorld @rx-angular/cdk remains 33/184, tslib remains 0/28 in both applications, and ngx-charts AJV remains 549/683. The current graph additions do not resolve every missing relation or supply new seeds.','- The prior angular-example-app result is reproduced exactly: 1,054 per-chunk and 1,075 cross-chunk, with identical recovered target-pair sets.','','## Files, verification and reproduction','','`per-library-per-chunk.csv` is the primary 25-row comparison; `per-library-cross-chunk.csv` is the separate 25-row cross-chunk comparison. CSV rates are fractions in [0,1]; report rates are percentages. Repository aggregates are in repos-per-chunk.csv and repos-cross-chunk.csv. Each subject has code-only relations, per-target traces, promotion rounds and graph provenance. `verification.json` records target/seed/hash equality and recovered-pair controls. Graph tests and simulation tests: 14 passed. Every propagation fixed point is checked against independent paired-graph BFS.','','Run from a fresh working/output copy (the runner refuses to overwrite completed subject summaries):','','```sh','node --test scripts/real-app/esbuild-propagation/edges.test.mjs scripts/real-app/connectivity/simulate.test.mjs','node --max-old-space-size=12288 scripts/real-app/esbuild-propagation/run-dataset.mjs realworld-apps--angular-realworld-example-app','node --max-old-space-size=12288 scripts/real-app/esbuild-propagation/run-dataset.mjs Ismaestro--angular-example-app','node --max-old-space-size=12288 scripts/real-app/esbuild-propagation/run-dataset.mjs swimlane--ngx-charts','python3 scripts/real-app/esbuild-propagation/report-dataset.py','```']
